[2026-09-29T15:25:45.617Z] [DEBUG] [guard:wasm] label_response input JSON (263107 bytes): {"capabilities":{},"tool_args":{"query":"repo:apache/cloudstack is:issue guest OS list version"},"tool_name":"search_issues","tool_result":{"content":[{"text":"{\"total_count\":294,\"incomplete_results\":false,\"items\":[{\"id\":5630698507,\"number\":14265,\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"[Feature] Add latest OS versions to guest OS list\",\"body\":\"### The required feature described as a wish\\n\\nAs an MSP switching from vmware to cloudstack at the moment we would love to see the latest Linux versions within the Guest OS list by default. Currently Alma/Rocky etc. are on version 9, debian latest is 12, ubuntu latest is 24. All of them have one newer Major version not sure about other distributions.\\n\\nI know we can add all these manual. But would be nice to have them in the default to have no issues wit future cloudstack updates.\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"la-wu\",\"id\":295070573,\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOEZZrbQ\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/295070573?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/la-wu\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/la-wu\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/la-wu/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/la-wu/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/la-wu/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/la-wu/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/la-wu/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/la-wu/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/la-wu/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/la-wu/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/la-wu/subscriptions\"},\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-29T12:39:54Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-29T12:39:54Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14265\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/14265\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14265/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14265/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14265/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack\",\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14265/reactions\"},\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAABT52kCw\"},{\"id\":5090153164,\"number\":13824,\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"Modernize the default Hyper-V enlightenment profile for Windows guests on KVM\",\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nApache CloudStack 4.22 gives all Windows guests a `localtime` clock and\\n`hypervclock`, but it emits a `\\u003chyperv\\u003e` feature block only when the guest OS\\nlabel contains `Windows PV`. Even in that case, the block is limited to:\\n\\n```xml\\n\\u003chyperv\\u003e\\n  \\u003crelaxed state='on'/\\u003e\\n  \\u003cvapic state='on'/\\u003e\\n  \\u003cspinlocks state='on' retries='8096'/\\u003e\\n\\u003c/hyperv\\u003e\\n```\\n\\nThis is a historical, very small subset of the Hyper-V enlightenments supported\\nby every KVM host family currently listed in the CloudStack 4.22 compatibility\\nmatrix. The generic `Windows PV` label also does not describe a Windows version\\nand does not, by itself, select VirtIO storage or networking.\\n\\nCloudStack should introduce an explicit, versioned Windows-on-KVM enlightenment\\nprofile instead of relying on the substring `Windows PV` as the only switch.\\n\\n## Current behavior\\n\\nIn `LibvirtComputingResource.enlightenWindowsVm()` CloudStack checks only:\\n\\n```java\\nif (vmTO.getOs().contains(\\\"Windows PV\\\")) {\\n    // relaxed, vapic and spinlocks only\\n}\\n```\\n\\n`LibvirtVMDef.HyperVEnlightenmentFeatureDef` can currently serialize only those\\nthree features. Separately, every OS label beginning with `Windows` receives a\\n`hypervclock` timer.\\n\\nConsequences:\\n\\n- Windows Server 2012 through Windows Server 2025 and current Windows desktop\\n  guests do not receive a `\\u003chyperv\\u003e` block when their real version-specific OS\\n  type is selected.\\n- Selecting `Windows PV` loses version information while enabling only three\\n  old enlightenments.\\n- The effective behavior is hard-coded rather than represented as a documented\\n  compatibility profile.\\n- CloudStack cannot safely add newer features according to host capabilities or\\n  preserve a stable feature set for live migration within a cluster.\\n\\n## Why this can be modernized without requiring VirtIO drivers\\n\\nHyper-V enlightenments are CPU/timer/interrupt interfaces exposed by KVM and\\nQEMU. They are independent of the guest's disk and network device models. A\\nWindows VM can use these features while continuing to boot from IDE or SATA and\\nusing an emulated E1000 NIC.\\n\\nThis issue therefore must not implicitly change disk controllers, NIC models,\\nfirmware, or machine type. Those changes have separate guest-driver and boot\\ncompatibility risks.\\n\\n## CloudStack 4.22 KVM compatibility floor\\n\\nThe 4.22 compatibility matrix lists the following KVM host OS families:\\n\\n- Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 LTS\\n- Oracle Linux, Rocky Linux, AlmaLinux and RHEL 8, 9 and 10\\n- openSUSE Leap 15 and SLES 15\\n\\nCloudStack documents major OS families and does not pin a minimum service-pack,\\npoint-release, kernel, QEMU package build, or libvirt package build. Therefore\\nthe table below is a conservative engineering floor based on the oldest branch\\nnamed by CloudStack, not a claim that every EOL initial point-release is tested\\nor should be deployed.\\n\\n| CloudStack 4.22 host family | Conservative oldest branch reference | QEMU family | libvirt family | Linux kernel family | Qualification |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|\\n| Ubuntu | 22.04 LTS | 6.2 | 8.0 | 5.15 | Explicitly listed by CloudStack |\\n| RHEL / Oracle Linux | 8.0-era baseline | 2.12 | 4.5 | 4.18 | RHEL is listed as expected to work; current patched minor releases are required in practice |\\n| Rocky / AlmaLinux | EL8 baseline | no lower than the EL8 floor | no lower than the EL8 floor | 4.18 | These distributions first shipped after EL8.0; use the lower EL8 family floor for design |\\n| openSUSE Leap / SLES | 15.0-era baseline | 2.11 | 4.0 | 4.12 | CloudStack says Leap 15.6 is the tested Leap release; the older numbers are only a conservative branch floor |\\n\\nThe lowest conservative host in that matrix is still substantially newer than\\nthe minimum required for the proposed baseline below.\\n\\n## Proposed implementation\\n\\n### 1. Add explicit profiles and version-based defaults\\n\\nAdd a saved Windows virtualization profile with four values:\\n\\n- `disabled`: no `\\u003chyperv\\u003e` block; retain the existing Windows clock handling.\\n- `legacy`: exactly the current `Windows PV` feature set: `relaxed`, `vapic`,\\n  and `spinlocks retries='8096'`.\\n- `modern-safe`: the CPU-vendor-neutral, cross-distro baseline described below.\\n- `auto`: `modern-safe` plus optional features supported by every eligible host\\n  in the selected KVM cluster.\\n\\nUse the following defaults for newly deployed VMs:\\n\\n| Selected guest OS | Default profile | Reason |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Windows 8/8.1/10/11 | `modern-safe` | Version-specific modern Windows type |\\n| Windows Server 2012/2012 R2/2016/2019/2022/2025 and newer | `modern-safe` | Version-specific modern Windows Server type |\\n| Windows 7 and Windows Server 2008/2008 R2 | `legacy` | Preserve the small feature set originally introduced for Windows Server 2008 and later |\\n| Windows Vista/XP, Windows Server 2003 and older | `disabled` | Do not advertise untested features to legacy guests |\\n| Versionless `Windows PV` | `legacy` | Preserve current CloudStack behavior |\\n| Unknown or unclassified Windows type | `disabled` | Prefer predictable compatibility when the Windows generation is not known |\\n\\nThe operator can override the proposed value before deployment. Existing VMs\\nmust keep their current generated XML when no saved profile exists: existing\\n`Windows PV` VMs continue to behave as `legacy`, while other existing Windows\\nVMs continue without a `\\u003chyperv\\u003e` block. An upgrade alone must not alter a VM's\\nvirtual CPU definition.\\n\\nThe selected and effective values must be visible in debug logs and in the\\ngenerated domain XML.\\n\\n### 2. Expose a clear Windows-only UI and API setting\\n\\nShow a field labelled **Windows virtualization optimizations** when the selected\\nhypervisor is KVM and the selected guest OS is Windows. Hide it for non-Windows\\nguests and non-KVM hypervisors.\\n\\nThe field is automatically populated according to the table above and offers:\\n\\n- **Modern (recommended)** ??? portable modern optimizations supported across the\\n  CloudStack 4.22 KVM host baseline.\\n- **Automatic** ??? Modern plus additional optimizations supported by every host\\n  in the target KVM cluster.\\n- **Legacy compatibility** ??? current `Windows PV` behavior.\\n- **Disabled** ??? no Hyper-V feature block.\\n\\nThe management server must be the authoritative source for the supported\\nprofile values and their stable identifiers. The UI must populate the drop-down\\nfrom backend-provided values, following the same general pattern used for other\\nVM settings such as keyboard type and root disk controller. Do not maintain an\\nindependent frontend-only list that can drift from backend validation.\\n\\nThe default UI should not expose individual QEMU feature names or the raw\\nspinlock retry number. A tooltip or help panel must explain that the setting\\ncontrols Hyper-V-compatible CPU, timer, and interrupt optimizations exposed by\\nKVM; it does not install or require VirtIO storage or network drivers. Each\\noption must have a short description and a link to administrator documentation.\\n\\nStore the template's proposed/default value in template details. At deployment,\\ncopy the selected value to VM details. From that point, the VM value is the\\nauthoritative setting used for every start, restart, and reschedule. Changing it\\nafter deployment must require the VM to be stopped. This prevents a later\\nCloudStack upgrade, template edit, or move to another host from silently\\nchanging the virtual CPU definition.\\n\\nExpose the same drop-down in VM Settings. When the VM is stopped, an operator can\\nselect another backend-provided profile and save it to VM details. When the VM\\nis running, show the effective value as read-only and explain that the VM must\\nbe stopped before it can be changed. The newly selected profile is applied when\\nCloudStack next generates the domain XML and starts the VM.\\n\\nThe API must expose the supported values, accept the selected optional value at\\ndeployment, and provide an update operation for a stopped VM so API and UI\\nbehavior remain identical. Backend validation must reject unknown values and\\nchanges attempted while the VM is running. Existing callers that omit the value\\nretain the compatibility behavior described above.\\n\\n### 3. Implement a universal `modern-safe` baseline\\n\\nUse an explicit/custom feature list rather than libvirt Hyper-V passthrough:\\n\\n```xml\\n\\u003chyperv mode='custom'\\u003e\\n  \\u003crelaxed state='on'/\\u003e\\n  \\u003cvapic state='on'/\\u003e\\n  \\u003cspinlocks state='on' retries='4095'/\\u003e\\n  \\u003cvpindex state='on'/\\u003e\\n  \\u003cruntime state='on'/\\u003e\\n  \\u003csynic state='on'/\\u003e\\n  \\u003cstimer state='on'/\\u003e\\n\\u003c/hyperv\\u003e\\n```\\n\\nThe highest host requirement in this baseline is:\\n\\n- **QEMU 2.6 or newer**\\n- **libvirt 1.3.3 or newer**\\n\\nThis is below the conservative QEMU/libvirt floor of every KVM distribution\\nfamily listed by CloudStack 4.22. It is independent of Intel versus AMD host CPU\\nand does not require VirtIO drivers in the Windows guest.\\n\\n`spinlocks retries` is a retry count, not a time value or network port. When one\\nvirtual CPU is waiting for a lock potentially held by another virtual CPU, the\\nguest retries that many times before sending the advisory\\n`HvCallNotifyLongSpinWait` hypercall. The notification helps the hypervisor make\\na better scheduling decision, especially on an overcommitted host where the\\nlock-holding virtual CPU may not currently be running.\\n\\nCloudStack introduced the decimal value `8096` in the 2018 enlightenment change,\\nbut its commit, pull request, tests, and review discussion contain no explanation\\nfor that value. There is no technical relationship between this retry count and\\nCloudStack's optional integration API port 8096; the identical decimal number\\nappears to be coincidental. Preserve `8096` only in the `legacy` profile so that\\nexisting behavior remains reproducible. Use `4095` (`0xfff`) for `modern-safe`,\\nwhich is the current QEMU recommendation for overcommitted hosts. QEMU documents\\n`0xffffffff` as the effective \\\"never notify\\\" choice when this scheduling hint is\\nnot desired.\\n\\n### 4. Add newer features through the `auto` profile\\n\\nDo not add the following to the unconditional baseline:\\n\\n| Optional feature | Minimum libvirt | Minimum QEMU | Proposed policy |\\n|---|---:|---:|---|\\n| `frequencies` | 4.7.0 | 2.12 | `auto` tier only; required dependency for re-enlightenment |\\n| `reenlightenment` | 4.7.0 | 3.0 | `auto` tier; validate migration behavior and CPU frequency exposure |\\n| `tlbflush` | 4.7.0 | 3.0 | `auto` tier; requires `vpindex` |\\n| `ipi` | 4.10.0 | 3.1 | `auto` tier; requires `vpindex` |\\n| `stimer direct` | 5.7.0 | 4.1 | Newer-host tier only |\\n| `evmcs` | 4.10.0 | 3.1 | Explicit opt-in only for nested Hyper-V on compatible Intel hosts; not a universal Intel/AMD feature |\\n| `avic` | 8.10.0 | 6.2 | Do not enable generically; hardware/topology-specific |\\n| `tlbflush direct/extended` | 11.0.0 | 7.1 | Future tier only; outside the oldest CloudStack 4.22 host-family floor |\\n\\nFeature dependencies must be encoded and tested, for example `stimer` depends\\non `synic`, `synic` depends on `vpindex`, and `reenlightenment` depends on\\n`frequencies`.\\n\\nThe `modern-safe` profile must not perform Intel/AMD or per-host capability\\nchecks. It is the portable baseline.\\n\\nThe `auto` profile is part of this proposal and may be delivered as a follow-up\\nPR after the portable baseline and UI/API setting. It must use the intersection\\nof libvirt/QEMU capabilities across every host eligible to run the VM. Store both\\nthe requested value (`auto`) and the resolved feature list on the VM so that its\\nvirtual CPU definition remains stable across restart and migration. If a target\\nhost cannot provide that saved feature list, CloudStack must reject that target\\nrather than silently reducing the list.\\n\\n`mode='passthrough'` must not be used because it can expose a different feature\\nset on different hosts and make live migration unsafe. Optional features with\\nadditional hardware requirements, including `evmcs`, `avic`, and\\n`reenlightenment`, must not be enabled merely because the installed QEMU version\\nrecognizes their XML.\\n\\n### 5. Extend the domain XML model and Windows classification\\n\\n- Extend `HyperVEnlightenmentFeatureDef` to serialize the baseline and optional\\n  feature set, including nested attributes only where required.\\n- Replace the single `contains(\\\"Windows PV\\\")` decision with guest-family and\\n  guest-version-aware selection.\\n- Preserve `hypervclock` and existing local-time behavior.\\n- Persist the chosen/effective profile so rescheduling and restart generate the\\n  same virtual CPU definition.\\n- Reject an unsupported explicitly requested profile with a clear, actionable\\n  error; never silently reduce the requested feature set or emit XML the\\n  destination cluster cannot support.\\n\\n## Compatibility and rollout requirements\\n\\n- No change to an existing VM merely because CloudStack was upgraded.\\n- No automatic IDE/SATA-to-VirtIO, E1000-to-VirtIO, BIOS-to-UEFI, or\\n  i440FX-to-Q35 conversion as part of this issue.\\n- No dependence on VirtIO drivers.\\n- The baseline must work on both Intel and AMD KVM hosts.\\n- The effective feature set must be stable across all hosts eligible for live\\n  migration of the VM.\\n- Apply the version-based defaults only to newly deployed VMs. Preserve the\\n  generated XML of existing VMs unless the operator explicitly changes it.\\n- Document that changing a VM's enlightenment profile changes its virtual CPU\\n  definition and must be performed while stopped.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n1. Unit tests verify exact XML for `disabled`, `legacy`, `modern-safe`, and each\\n   supported `auto` capability tier.\\n2. Unit tests verify guest classification for version-specific Windows types,\\n   `Windows PV`, non-Windows guests, and null/unknown OS mappings.\\n3. The `modern-safe` XML can be defined and started on the oldest supported\\n   CloudStack CI images or equivalent test hosts for the Ubuntu 22.04, EL8,\\n   and SUSE 15 families.\\n4. Boot, reboot, clean shutdown, timekeeping, and multi-vCPU stress are tested\\n   with Windows Server 2012 R2, 2016, 2019, 2022, and 2025.\\n5. At least one test uses only emulated storage/network devices to prove that\\n   VirtIO drivers are not a prerequisite.\\n6. Intel and AMD hosts are covered.\\n7. Cold and live migration are tested within a homogeneous cluster and across\\n   hosts with different QEMU/libvirt patch levels but the same negotiated\\n   effective profile.\\n8. An existing VM without profile metadata retains the pre-change XML.\\n9. Unsupported optional features produce a clear validation error; CloudStack\\n   does not silently reduce a saved or explicitly selected feature set.\\n10. Administrator documentation describes profiles, host-version boundaries,\\n    guest-version mapping, override behavior, and rollback.\\n11. UI tests verify that the field is shown only for Windows on KVM, receives the\\n    correct version-based default, can be overridden, and includes explanatory\\n    help text.\\n12. Tests preserve `8096` in `legacy` and emit `4095` in `modern-safe`.\\n13. The VM Settings drop-down is populated from backend-provided values, is\\n    editable for a stopped VM, is read-only for a running VM, and persists the\\n    selected value in VM details.\\n14. API tests verify supported-value discovery, deployment-time selection,\\n    stopped-VM updates, rejection of unknown values, and rejection of changes\\n    while a VM is running.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n\\n- Selecting VirtIO disk or NIC models\\n- Installing or validating Windows VirtIO drivers\\n- Automatically converting existing disk controllers or firmware\\n- Changing BIOS/i440FX versus UEFI/Q35 defaults\\n- Video-device modernization\\n- Enabling nested Hyper-V or `evmcs` by default\\n\\n## References\\n\\n- [CloudStack 4.22 compatibility matrix](https://docs.cloudstack.apache.org/en/4.22.0.0/releasenotes/compat.html)\\n- [Current CloudStack KVM Windows feature and clock generation](https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/blob/4.22.0.0/plugins/hypervisors/kvm/src/main/java/com/cloud/hypervisor/kvm/resource/LibvirtComputingResource.java)\\n- [Current CloudStack Hyper-V feature XML model](https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/blob/4.22.0.0/plugins/hypervisors/kvm/src/main/java/com/cloud/hypervisor/kvm/resource/LibvirtVMDef.java)\\n- [Original CloudStack Windows enlightenment change](https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/commit/c4b621a418fe74a56e68140f1aa35c70562d7248)\\n- [libvirt domain XML: Hyper-V features and minimum versions](https://libvirt.org/formatdomain.html#hypervisor-features)\\n- [QEMU Hyper-V enlightenment behavior and recommendations](https://www.qemu.org/docs/master/system/i386/hyperv.html)\\n- [Microsoft Hyper-V guest spinlock behavior](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/virtualization/hyper-v-on-windows/tlfs/vp-properties)\\n- [Microsoft `HvCallNotifyLongSpinWait`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/virtualization/hyper-v-on-windows/tlfs/hypercalls/hvcallnotifylongspinwait)\\n- [Ubuntu 22.04 QEMU package](https://packages.ubuntu.com/jammy/qemu-system-x86)\\n- [Ubuntu 22.04 libvirt package](https://packages.ubuntu.com/jammy/admin/libvirt-daemon-system)\\n\\n## Decisions proposed by this issue\\n\\n- Default new, version-specific Windows 8 / Server 2012 and newer VMs to\\n  `modern-safe`; default older and unknown types according to the explicit table\\n  above.\\n- Show a documented, operator-overridable Windows-only setting in both the UI\\n  and API.\\n- Populate the UI drop-down from the backend's authoritative profile list and\\n  allow the saved value to be changed from VM Settings while the VM is stopped.\\n- Save the template default and copy the selected value to the VM so subsequent\\n  starts use the same virtual CPU definition.\\n- Ship the CPU-vendor-neutral `modern-safe` baseline without host capability\\n  negotiation.\\n- Include `auto` in the overall issue scope, but allow its cluster capability\\n  implementation to be a follow-up PR.\\n- Preserve retries `8096` only for exact legacy compatibility and use QEMU's\\n  documented overcommit recommendation, `4095`, for `modern-safe`.\\r\\n\",\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"andrijapanicsb\",\"id\":45762285,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NzYyMjg1\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45762285?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/andrijapanicsb\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/subscriptions\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":584072971,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:kvm\",\"name\":\"component:kvm\",\"color\":\"006b75\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWw1ODQwNzI5NzE=\"},{\"id\":584074312,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:libvirt\",\"name\":\"component:libvirt\",\"color\":\"bfdadc\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWw1ODQwNzQzMTI=\"},{\"id\":739374767,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:UI\",\"name\":\"component:UI\",\"color\":\"ea62a8\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzkzNzQ3Njc=\"}],\"assignee\":{\"login\":\"andrijapanicsb\",\"id\":45762285,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NzYyMjg1\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45762285?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/andrijapanicsb\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/subscriptions\"},\"comments\":3,\"created_at\":\"2026-08-07T12:29:56Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-18T12:23:16Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13824\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/13824\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13824/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13824/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13824/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack\",\"milestone\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/47\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/47\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/47/labels\",\"id\":15843055,\"number\":47,\"state\":\"open\",\"title\":\"24.0\",\"description\":\"\",\"creator\":{\"login\":\"weizhouapache\",\"id\":57355700,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MzU1NzAw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57355700?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/weizhouapache\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/subscriptions\"},\"open_issues\":272,\"closed_issues\":36,\"created_at\":\"2026-05-08T06:15:20Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-29T10:27:41Z\",\"node_id\":\"MI_kwDOAJTq2M4A8b7v\"},\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13824/reactions\"},\"assignees\":[{\"login\":\"andrijapanicsb\",\"id\":45762285,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NzYyMjg1\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45762285?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/andrijapanicsb\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/subscriptions\"}],\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAABL2WSzA\",\"type\":{\"id\":93574,\"node_id\":\"IT_kwDNuP_OAAFthg\",\"name\":\"Feature\",\"description\":\"A request, idea, or new functionality\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"created_at\":\"2024-01-25T09:11:09Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2024-10-08T08:30:20Z\"}},{\"id\":4136813241,\"number\":12889,\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"Windows Guest Instances Have No Sound\",\"body\":\"### problem\\n\\nWindows guest instances (Virtual Desktops) do not find any Audio hardware.\\n\\n\\u003cimg width=\\\"351\\\" height=\\\"158\\\" alt=\\\"Image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/350cc7cf-e758-497e-8615-c0851773fd17\\\" /\\u003e\\n\\nBy adding `sound` to the global setting `allow.additional.vm.configuration.list.kvm`...\\n\\n\\u003cimg width=\\\"1390\\\" height=\\\"124\\\" alt=\\\"Image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f7430d0d-d65f-4719-8ab4-c69579b7af11\\\" /\\u003e\\n\\n...CloudMonkey can add this `extraconfig`.\\n\\n\\u003cimg width=\\\"1009\\\" height=\\\"106\\\" alt=\\\"Image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2eeb6821-69ed-4b9c-b5e7-fbeeb37aba95\\\" /\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cimg width=\\\"515\\\" height=\\\"436\\\" alt=\\\"Image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a1f42fad-9a33-46db-b6c5-bb2237693cf5\\\" /\\u003e\\n\\nThen, after power cycling the VM, the issue is resolved.\\n\\n\\u003cimg width=\\\"254\\\" height=\\\"121\\\" alt=\\\"Image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/606a92e2-3a94-43c2-a3d4-2c7d9e858f9a\\\" /\\u003e\\n\\nIt does not feel like a feature request, but a \\\"bug\\\" to the default global settings.\",\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"daviftorres\",\"id\":90287660,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjkwMjg3NjYw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90287660?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/daviftorres\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/daviftorres\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/daviftorres/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/daviftorres/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/daviftorres/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/daviftorres/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/daviftorres/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/daviftorres/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/daviftorres/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/daviftorres/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/daviftorres/subscriptions\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":37843366,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:enhancement\",\"name\":\"type:enhancement\",\"color\":\"84b6eb\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzg0MzM2Ng==\"},{\"id\":584072971,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:kvm\",\"name\":\"component:kvm\",\"color\":\"006b75\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWw1ODQwNzI5NzE=\"},{\"id\":739374767,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:UI\",\"name\":\"component:UI\",\"color\":\"ea62a8\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzkzNzQ3Njc=\"}],\"assignee\":{\"login\":\"sureshanaparti\",\"id\":12028987,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDI4OTg3\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12028987?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/sureshanaparti\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/subscriptions\"},\"comments\":8,\"created_at\":\"2026-03-25T16:35:42Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-14T14:00:22Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/12889\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/12889\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/12889/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/12889/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/12889/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack\",\"milestone\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/45\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/45\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/45/labels\",\"id\":14595362,\"number\":45,\"state\":\"open\",\"title\":\"4.20.4\",\"creator\":{\"login\":\"DaanHoogland\",\"id\":2486961,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODY5NjE=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2486961?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/DaanHoogland\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/subscriptions\"},\"open_issues\":135,\"closed_issues\":79,\"created_at\":\"2026-01-21T11:18:05Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-15T19:56:19Z\",\"node_id\":\"MI_kwDOAJTq2M4A3rUi\"},\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/12889/reactions\"},\"assignees\":[{\"login\":\"sureshanaparti\",\"id\":12028987,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDI4OTg3\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12028987?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/sureshanaparti\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/subscriptions\"}],\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOAJTq2M72ksK5\"},{\"id\":3803910012,\"number\":12405,\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"[KVM] Restored backup volume not attached to running VM via libvirt - only database updated\",\"body\":\"### problem\\n\\n## Description\\nWhen restoring a volume from backup and attaching it to a **running** KVM VM, the volume is only attached at the **database level** but not actually hot-attached to the running VM via libvirt. This means:\\n1. The volume appears in CloudStack UI as \\\"attached\\\"\\n2. The volume does NOT appear in `virsh domblklist \\u003cvm-name\\u003e` \\n3. The volume is NOT visible inside the guest OS\\n4. User must reboot(forced) the VM to see the restored volume\\n## Root Cause\\nIn `KVMGuru.attachRestoredVolumeToVirtualMachine()` (line 380-400), the method only:\\n- Updates the volume state in the database via `_volumeDao.attachVolume()`\\n- Sets volume state to `Ready`\\nIt does **NOT**:\\n- Check if VM is running\\n- Send an `AttachCommand` to the KVM agent to hot-attach the disk via libvirt\\n## Expected Behavior\\nWhen attaching a restored volume to a **running** VM:\\n1. CloudStack should detect the VM state\\n2. If VM is [Running](cci:1://file:///root/new_merge/olympos-cloud-platform/plugins/hypervisors/kvm/src/main/java/com/cloud/hypervisor/kvm/resource/LibvirtComputingResource.java:5982:4-5991:5), send a libvirt attach command to hot-attach the disk\\n3. Volume should immediately appear in `virsh domblklist` and inside guest OS\\n4. No reboot should be required\\n\\n### versions\\n\\nCloudStack: 4.21.0\\nHypervisor: KVM\\nHost OS: Rocky Linux 9\\nGuest OS: Rocky Linux 9 / Windows 10 - 2022 Server\\n\\n\\n### The steps to reproduce the bug\\n\\n## Steps to Reproduce\\n1. Create a VM with a data disk\\n2. Create a backup of the VM\\n3. Start the VM (ensure it's running)\\n4. Restore the backed-up volume and attach to the running VM via API:\\n   `restoreVolumeFromBackupAndAttachToVM`\\n5. Check `virsh domblklist \\u003cvm-name\\u003e` on the KVM host\\n6. **Observe:** The restored volume is NOT listed\\n7. Check inside guest OS\\n8. **Observe:** The disk is NOT visible\\n9. Reboot(forced) the VM\\n10. **Observe:** After reboot(forced), the disk appears\\n\\n### What to do about it?\\n\\nEither:\\nA) Add hot-attach logic to `KVMGuru.attachRestoredVolumeToVirtualMachine()` to send `AttachCommand` when VM is running\\nB) Or document this as expected behavior and require users to stop VM before restoring volumes\\nOption A is preferred as it aligns with how regular [attachVolume](cci:1://file:///root/new_merge/olympos-cloud-platform/server/src/main/java/com/cloud/storage/VolumeApiServiceImpl.java:2479:4-2483:5) API works for running VMs.\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"furkandogmus\",\"id\":69652349,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NjUyMzQ5\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69652349?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/furkandogmus\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/furkandogmus\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/furkandogmus/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/furkandogmus/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/furkandogmus/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/furkandogmus/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/furkandogmus/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/furkandogmus/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/furkandogmus/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/furkandogmus/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/furkandogmus/subscriptions\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":1155016910,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/status:needs-reproducing\",\"name\":\"status:needs-reproducing\",\"color\":\"4e62fc\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTU1MDE2OTEw\"}],\"comments\":3,\"created_at\":\"2026-01-12T11:28:53Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-24T11:51:32Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/12405\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/12405\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/12405/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/12405/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/12405/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack\",\"milestone\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/46\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/46\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/46/labels\",\"id\":15514689,\"number\":46,\"state\":\"open\",\"title\":\"4.22.2\",\"description\":\"\",\"creator\":{\"login\":\"sureshanaparti\",\"id\":12028987,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDI4OTg3\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12028987?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/sureshanaparti\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/subscriptions\"},\"open_issues\":252,\"closed_issues\":114,\"created_at\":\"2026-04-13T07:02:43Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-29T13:13:59Z\",\"node_id\":\"MI_kwDOAJTq2M4A7LxB\"},\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":3,\"+1\":2,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":1,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/12405/reactions\"},\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOAJTq2M7iuw98\",\"type\":{\"id\":93570,\"node_id\":\"IT_kwDNuP_OAAFtgg\",\"name\":\"Bug\",\"description\":\"An unexpected problem or behavior\",\"color\":\"red\",\"created_at\":\"2024-01-25T09:11:09Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2024-07-26T10:04:57Z\"}},{\"id\":2020923395,\"number\":8294,\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"Is it possible to add ipv6 to a deployed Shared network?\",\"body\":\"\\u003c!--\\r\\nVerify first that your issue/request is not already reported on GitHub.\\r\\nAlso test if the latest release and main branch are affected too.\\r\\nAlways add information AFTER of these HTML comments, but no need to delete the comments.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n##### ISSUE TYPE\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Pick one below and delete the rest --\\u003e\\r\\n * Other / Question\\r\\n\\r\\n##### COMPONENT NAME\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nCategorize the issue, e.g. API, VR, VPN, UI, etc.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nNetwork\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nNew line separated list of affected versions, commit ID for issues on main branch.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nCloudStack 4.18.1.0\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### CONFIGURATION\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nInformation about the configuration if relevant, e.g. basic network, advanced networking, etc.  N/A otherwise\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nNetwork in advanced core zone\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nN/A\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n##### SUMMARY\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly --\\u003e\\r\\nCan you tell me if it is possible to add ipv6 to a deployed Shared network in an advanced core zone if the fields related to ipv6 were not filled in during its creation. Perhaps this can be achieved by editing the database? The important point is that there are already deployed vms in the network and their operability should not be disturbed. \\r\\n\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"0sorkon\",\"id\":3714094,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MTQwOTQ=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3714094?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/0sorkon\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/subscriptions\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":37843368,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:question\",\"name\":\"type:question\",\"color\":\"cc317c\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzg0MzM2OA==\"},{\"id\":584073336,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:ipv6\",\"name\":\"component:ipv6\",\"color\":\"c2e0c6\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWw1ODQwNzMzMzY=\"},{\"id\":817420428,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:improvement\",\"name\":\"type:improvement\",\"color\":\"a5f9ff\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWw4MTc0MjA0Mjg=\"},{\"id\":1663969521,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/Severity:Major\",\"name\":\"Severity:Major\",\"color\":\"903636\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWwxNjYzOTY5NTIx\"},{\"id\":2531620643,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/complexity:complex\",\"name\":\"complexity:complex\",\"color\":\"0000cc\",\"description\":\"a few weeks to a few months of work with a lot of interaction\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWwyNTMxNjIwNjQz\"},{\"id\":4507982790,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/ipv6\",\"name\":\"ipv6\",\"color\":\"C744C9\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAABDLJbxg\"},{\"id\":9851088157,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/long-term-plan\",\"name\":\"long-term-plan\",\"color\":\"aaaaaa\",\"description\":\"remove this label if you plan to pick up this issue.\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAACSyutHQ\"}],\"comments\":11,\"created_at\":\"2023-12-01T13:51:35Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-01T07:27:02Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8294\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/8294\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8294/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8294/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8294/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack\",\"milestone\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/19\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19/labels\",\"id\":6265435,\"number\":19,\"state\":\"open\",\"title\":\"unplanned\",\"creator\":{\"login\":\"DaanHoogland\",\"id\":2486961,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODY5NjE=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2486961?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/DaanHoogland\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/subscriptions\"},\"open_issues\":185,\"closed_issues\":1302,\"created_at\":\"2021-01-04T09:07:50Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-24T11:01:33Z\",\"node_id\":\"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lNjI2NTQzNQ==\"},\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8294/reactions\"},\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOAJTq2M54dNgD\",\"type\":{\"id\":93574,\"node_id\":\"IT_kwDNuP_OAAFthg\",\"name\":\"Feature\",\"description\":\"A request, idea, or new functionality\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"created_at\":\"2024-01-25T09:11:09Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2024-10-08T08:30:20Z\"}},{\"id\":2611976842,\"number\":9853,\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"Network-\\u003eSecurity groups not shown after wizard\",\"body\":\"\\u003c!--\\r\\nVerify first that your issue/request is not already reported on GitHub.\\r\\nAlso test if the latest release and main branch are affected too.\\r\\nAlways add information AFTER of these HTML comments, but no need to delete the comments.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n##### ISSUE TYPE\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Pick one below and delete the rest --\\u003e\\r\\n * Bug Report\\r\\n\\r\\n##### COMPONENT NAME\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nCategorize the issue, e.g. API, VR, VPN, UI, etc.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nUI\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nNew line separated list of affected versions, commit ID for issues on main branch.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n4.19.1.2\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### CONFIGURATION\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nInformation about the configuration if relevant, e.g. basic network, advanced networking, etc.  N/A otherwise\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\nbasic network, with security group offering\\r\\n\\r\\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\nalmalinux9, kvm\\r\\n\\r\\n##### SUMMARY\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter a fresh install and doing the setup wizard, the Network-\\u003eSecurity groups UI item will not be shown until you restart\\r\\nthe cloudstack-management service and relog. \\r\\n\\r\\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\\r\\n\\u003c!--\\r\\nFor bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case. Use Screenshots if accurate.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor new features, show how the feature would be used.\\r\\n--\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Paste example playbooks or commands between quotes below --\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nDo a fresh CloudStack install\\r\\nRun through the wizard with basic zone + security groups\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- You can also paste gist.github.com links for larger files --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\\r\\n\\u003c!-- What did you expect to happen when running the steps above? --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nSecurity group entry without restarting the cloudstack-management service.\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\\r\\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\\r\\n\\u003c!-- What actually happened? --\\u003e\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003c!-- Paste verbatim command output between quotes below --\\u003e\\r\\n~~~\\r\\nSecurity groups item is missing, and maybe other too?(Guest VLAN)\\r\\n~~~\\r\\n\",\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"user\":{\"login