connect","updated_at":"2026-09-17T13:36:00Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/10011","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/468252?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maic/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maic/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maic","id":468252,"login":"maic","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2ODI1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maic/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maic/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maic/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maic/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maic"}},{"author_association":"NONE","body":"### problem\n\nHi.\nIn a advanced netowrk zone, VXLAN based, my KVM agents are using the storage network address as private ip address.\n\nThe network storage network is not routable between components, and it is causing severe problems like mal function on CPVM that try to connect on the wrong address to establish a connection with the hypervisor VNC Port.\n\nThe storage address is correctly found.\n\nThis is an exemple of my interfaces config:\n\n```\nroot@hypr2-rck3:~# ip -br a\nlo               UNKNOWN        127.0.0.1/8 10.1.4.2/32 fd00:1337:1:4::2/128 ::1/128 \nens8f0np0        DOWN           \nens8f1np1        DOWN           \nens5f0np0        UP             10.1.32.3/31 fd00:1337:1:20::3/127 fe80::e4f8:1110:2c37:62ca/64 \nens5f1np1        DOWN           \nvxlan200         UNKNOWN        \nvxlan202         UNKNOWN        \nv-secstorbr@v-secstor UP             \nv-secstor@v-secstorbr UP             10.1.48.2/22 fd00:1337:1:2d::2/64 fe80::a6c6:ac43:1c4:ab35/64 \nv-clmgmtbr@v-clmgmt UP             \nv-clmgmt@v-clmgmtbr UP             10.1.0.2/22 fd00:1337:1::2/64 fe80::a535:f84c:40f1:b424/64 \neth-clguest      UNKNOWN        \nv-clstoragebr@v-clstorage UP             \nv-clstorage@v-clstoragebr UP             10.1.16.2/20 fd00:1337:1:10::2/64 fe80::e263:1ef4:9243:237e/64 \nbr-secstor       UP             \neth-clpublic     UNKNOWN        \nvxlan100         UNKNOWN        \nbr-clmgmt        UP             \nbr-clguest       UP             \nbr-clstorage     UP             \nbr-clpublic      UP             \ncloud0           UNKNOWN        169.254.0.1/16 fe80::d028:d0ff:fe30:3c0d/64\n```\n\n\nagent.properties\n```\nroot@hypr2-rck3:~# cat /etc/cloudstack/agent/agent.properties\n#Storage\n#Tue Jun 30 18:10:35 BRT 2026\nLibvirtComputingResource.id=6\nLibvirtComputingResource.name=hypr2-rck3\nLibvirtComputingResource.uuid=***\ncluster=1\ndomr.scripts.dir=scripts/network/domr/kvm\nguest.cpu.mode=custom\nguest.cpu.model=Icelake-Server-noTSX\nguest.network.device=br-clguest\nguid=d46e7512-0114-378f-baf5-0c0683092c05\nhost=10.254.0.101,10.254.0.100@roundrobin\nhypervisor.type=kvm\niscsi.session.cleanup.enabled=false\nkeystore.passphrase=****\nlocal.storage.uuid=***\nnetwork.bridge.type=native\npod=1\nport=8250\nprivate.network.device=br-clmgmt\npublic.network.device=br-clpublic\nresource=com.cloud.hypervisor.kvm.resource.LibvirtComputingResource\nvm.migrate.wait=3600\nvxlan.network.vtep.ip=10.1.4.2\nworkers=5\nzone=2\n```\n\nThe agent is selecting 10.1.16.2 address as storage (correct) and private (incorrect, the correct IP should be 10.1.0.2).\n\nThis range is directly routable. The agent can reach the management servers from this address, and the management servers can do stablish new connections with hosts too.\n\nThere is some property that I can change to enforce the private address?\n\n### versions\n\nCloudstack 4.22.1.0\nOS: Rocky Linux 10.2\nAgent: 4.22.1.0\nJava: OpenJDK 64-Bit Server VM (Red_Hat-21.0.11.0.10-1) (build 21.0.11+10-LTS, mixed mode, sharing)\n\n\n### The steps to reproduce the bug\n\n1. Setup a FRR / VXLAN / EVPN enviroment\n2. Setup an advanced network zone in Cloudstack.\n3. Adopt an hypervisor (using the correct ip address on the UI).\n4. Adotion will work and hypervisor will be connected, able to run VMs, but with management IP incorrectly stored.\n\n\n\n### What to do about it?\n\n_No response_","comments":8,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13519/comments","created_at":"2026-06-30T23:32:52Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13519/events","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/13519","id":4781110245,"labels":[{"color":"fc2929","default":false,"description":"","id":37843364,"name":"type:bug","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzg0MzM2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:bug"},{"color":"006b75","default":false,"description":"","id":584072971,"name":"component:kvm","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1ODQwNzI5NzE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:kvm"},{"color":"f9d0c4","default":false,"description":"","id":592559219,"name":"component:networking","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1OTI1NTkyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:networking"},{"color":"906666","default":false,"description":"","id":1391968610,"name":"Severity:Minor","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzkxOTY4NjEw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/Severity:Minor"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13519/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":{"closed_issues":114,"created_at":"2026-04-13T07:02:43Z","creator":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12028987?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sureshanaparti","id":12028987,"login":"sureshanaparti","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDI4OTg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti"},"description":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/46","id":15514689,"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/46/labels","node_id":"MI_kwDOAJTq2M4A7LxB","number":46,"open_issues":252,"state":"open","title":"4.22.2","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:13:59Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/46"},"node_id":"I_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAABHPnz5Q","number":13519,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13519/reactions"},"repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack","state":"open","title":"HVM Agent selects wrong address for private_ip_address","updated_at":"2026-08-20T13:47:52Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13519","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/994671?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EduFrazao/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EduFrazao/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EduFrazao/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EduFrazao/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/EduFrazao","id":994671,"login":"EduFrazao","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NDY3MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EduFrazao/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EduFrazao/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EduFrazao/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EduFrazao/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EduFrazao/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EduFrazao"}},{"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"\u003c!--\r\nVerify first that your issue/request is not already reported on GitHub.\r\nAlso test if the latest release and main branch are affected too.\r\nAlways add information AFTER of these HTML comments, but no need to delete the comments.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n##### ISSUE TYPE\r\n\u003c!-- Pick one below and delete the rest --\u003e\r\n * Feature Idea\r\n\r\n##### COMPONENT NAME\r\n\u003c!--\r\nCategorize the issue, e.g. API, VR, VPN, UI, etc.\r\n--\u003e\r\n~~~\r\nVR\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\r\n\u003c!--\r\nNew line separated list of affected versions, commit ID for issues on main branch.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n4.20\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CONFIGURATION\r\n\u003c!--\r\nInformation about the configuration if relevant, e.g. basic network, advanced networking, etc.  N/A otherwise\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n\r\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\r\n\u003c!--\r\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n\r\n##### SUMMARY\r\n\u003c!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly --\u003e\r\n\r\nCurrent VR only resolve its own Guest Network DNS zone record and external records. When two or more peered VPC network, user has to manage the host resolution either by host file or create another forwarder point to VR in upstream DNS. I would say it would be more useful if we populate all DNS record across each peered zone VR with proper domain suffix. So the user do not need to discover new IP changes from peered zone.\r\n\r\n\r\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\r\n\u003c!--\r\nFor bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case. Use Screenshots if accurate.\r\n\r\nFor new features, show how the feature would be used.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- Paste example playbooks or commands between quotes below --\u003e\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- You can also paste gist.github.com links for larger files --\u003e\r\n\r\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\r\n\u003c!-- What did you expect to happen when running the steps above? --\u003e\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\r\n\u003c!-- What actually happened? --\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- Paste verbatim command output between quotes below --\u003e\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n","comments":4,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8627/comments","created_at":"2024-02-08T11:54:55Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8627/events","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/8627","id":2125006110,"labels":[{"color":"4471c4","default":false,"description":"","id":1150675549,"name":"type:new-feature","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTUwNjc1NTQ5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:new-feature"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8627/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":{"closed_issues":1302,"created_at":"2021-01-04T09:07:50Z","creator":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2486961?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DaanHoogland","id":2486961,"login":"DaanHoogland","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODY5NjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland"},"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/19","id":6265435,"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19/labels","node_id":"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lNjI2NTQzNQ==","number":19,"open_issues":185,"state":"open","title":"unplanned","updated_at":"2026-09-24T11:01:33Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19"},"node_id":"I_kwDOAJTq2M5-qQUe","number":8627,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8627/reactions"},"repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack","state":"open","title":"DNS resolution across VPCs connected via S2S VPN","updated_at":"2026-09-15T01:44:35Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8627","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36956864?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/levindecaro","id":36956864,"login":"levindecaro","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2OTU2ODY0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro"}},{"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"\u003c!--\r\nVerify first that your issue/request is not already reported on GitHub.\r\nAlso test if the latest release and main branch are affected too.\r\nAlways add information AFTER of these HTML comments, but no need to delete the comments.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n##### ISSUE TYPE\r\n\u003c!-- Pick one below and delete the rest --\u003e\r\n * Feature Idea\r\n\r\n##### COMPONENT NAME\r\n\u003c!--\r\nCategorize the issue, e.g. API, VR, VPN, UI, etc.\r\n--\u003e\r\n~~~\r\nUI,API,Guest Network\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\r\n\u003c!--\r\nNew line separated list of affected versions, commit ID for issues on main branch.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n~~~\r\nN/A\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CONFIGURATION\r\n\u003c!--\r\nInformation about the configuration if relevant, e.g. basic network, advanced networking, etc.  N/A otherwise\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n\r\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\r\n\u003c!--\r\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n\r\n##### SUMMARY\r\n\u003c!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly --\u003e\r\n\r\nWhen a Guest Network was created, the port forward and load balancer features only allow to be configure with pre-existing VM in same Guest Network. Sometime user will deploy self managed virtual ip address to support their application such as keepalived, MetalLB..etc. Today, the user will add a secondary NIC to the one of VM instance and then use the assigned NIC ip address to treat the virtual ip setup. Most of the time, it is unavoidable to use this appoarch when LB pool health check limit to L4 port checking. \r\n\r\nI'm wondering if ACS can implement IPAM management abstract under guest network to allow user create IP entities which will able to include into port forwarding or Load balancer member.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\r\n\u003c!--\r\nFor bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case. Use Screenshots if accurate.\r\n\r\nFor new features, show how the feature would be used.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- Paste example playbooks or commands between quotes below --\u003e\r\n~~~\r\nN/A\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- You can also paste gist.github.com links for larger files --\u003e\r\n\r\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\r\n\u003c!-- What did you expect to happen when running the steps above? --\u003e\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\r\n\u003c!-- What actually happened? --\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- Paste verbatim command output between quotes below --\u003e\r\n~~~\r\nN/A\r\n~~~\r\n","comments":5,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6163/comments","created_at":"2022-03-25T08:20:22Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6163/events","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/6163","id":1180482852,"labels":[{"color":"f9d0c4","default":false,"description":"","id":592559219,"name":"component:networking","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1OTI1NTkyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:networking"},{"color":"4471c4","default":false,"description":"","id":1150675549,"name":"type:new-feature","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTUwNjc1NTQ5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:new-feature"},{"color":"951862","default":false,"description":"","id":2630836378,"name":"status:needs-functional-definition","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjMwODM2Mzc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/status:needs-functional-definition"},{"color":"E43179","default":false,"description":"","id":6890295339,"name":"status:stale","node_id":"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAABmrGQKw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/status:stale"},{"color":"ededed","default":false,"id":9849008471,"name":"no-issue-activity","node_id":"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAACSwvxVw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/no-issue-activity"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6163/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":{"closed_issues":1302,"created_at":"2021-01-04T09:07:50Z","creator":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2486961?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DaanHoogland","id":2486961,"login":"DaanHoogland","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODY5NjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland"},"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/19","id":6265435,"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19/labels","node_id":"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lNjI2NTQzNQ==","number":19,"open_issues":185,"state":"open","title":"unplanned","updated_at":"2026-09-24T11:01:33Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19"},"node_id":"I_kwDOAJTq2M5GXL0k","number":6163,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6163/reactions"},"repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack","state":"open","title":"Add Support IPAM object to Allow Load Balancer or Port-forward map to floating IP Address","type":{"color":"blue","created_at":"2024-01-25T09:11:09Z","description":"A request, idea, or new functionality","id":93574,"name":"Feature","node_id":"IT_kwDNuP_OAAFthg","updated_at":"2024-10-08T08:30:20Z"},"updated_at":"2026-05-19T02:18:08Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6163","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36956864?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/levindecaro","id":36956864,"login":"levindecaro","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2OTU2ODY0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro"}},{"author_association":"NONE","body":"### problem\n\n\u003cp class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\" data-sourcepos=\"39:1-43:55;1334-1737\"\u003eWhen creating a CKS Kubernetes cluster and \u003cstrong\u003eexplicitly selecting a non-default node\ntemplate\u003c/strong\u003e (the stock \u003ccode class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\"\u003ecks-ubuntu-2204-kvm\u003c/code\u003e CKS-ready image) in Advanced Settings, the\nnode \u003cstrong\u003eInstance\u003c/strong\u003e stays in the \u003ccode class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\"\u003eStarting\u003c/code\u003e \u003cstrong\u003eVM lifecycle state\u003c/strong\u003e indefinitely and never\ntransitions to \u003ccode class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\"\u003eRunning\u003c/code\u003e — even though the libvirt domain is actually up on the KVM host\n(the VNC console is reachable and the guest OS boots).\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\" data-sourcepos=\"45:1-49:52;1739-2127\"\u003eThe same cluster creation \u003cstrong\u003esucceeds\u003c/strong\u003e when the \u003cstrong\u003edefault SystemVM template\u003c/strong\u003e\n(\u003ccode class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\"\u003esystemvm-kvm-4.22.0-x86_64\u003c/code\u003e) is used for the nodes. The only changed variable between\nthe working and failing cases is the node template selection, which points at the\n\u003cstrong\u003eFlexible Kubernetes Clusters per-node template selection path\u003c/strong\u003e rather than at\nin-guest provisioning (cloud-init / kubeadm / CNI).\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003ch2 class=\"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold\" data-sourcepos=\"55:1-55:22;2375-2396\"\u003eSTEPS TO REPRODUCE\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\u003col class=\"[li_\u0026amp;]:mb-0 [li_\u0026amp;]:mt-1 [li_\u0026amp;]:gap-1 [\u0026amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [\u0026amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3\" data-sourcepos=\"57:1-68:24;2398-3079\"\u003e\n\u003cli class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\" data-sourcepos=\"57:1-57:37;2398-2434\"\u003eACS 4.22.1.0 on KVM, CKS enabled.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\" data-sourcepos=\"58:1-59:21;2435-2538\"\u003eRegister the stock CKS-ready Ubuntu 22.04 KVM template (\u003ccode class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\"\u003ecks-ubuntu-2204-kvm\u003c/code\u003e),\nmarked \"For CKS\".\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\" data-sourcepos=\"60:1-60:57;2539-2595\"\u003eRegister a supported Kubernetes binaries ISO/version.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\" data-sourcepos=\"61:1-63:13;2596-2780\"\u003eCreate a CloudManaged Kubernetes cluster (3 control node HA) on a \u003cstrong\u003eVPC tier\u003c/strong\u003e network,\nand in \u003cstrong\u003eAdvanced Settings explicitly select \u003ccode class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\"\u003ecks-ubuntu-2204-kvm\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e as the node\ntemplate.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\" data-sourcepos=\"64:1-65:27;2781-2886\"\u003eObserve the control node Instance in the UI (Instances → the control node):\nit stays in \u003ccode class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\"\u003eStarting\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\" data-sourcepos=\"66:1-68:24;2887-3079\"\u003eRepeat the exact same cluster creation but \u003cstrong\u003edo not select a template\u003c/strong\u003e (use the\ndefault \u003ccode class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\"\u003esystemvm-kvm-4.22.0-x86_64\u003c/code\u003e): the node reaches \u003ccode class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\"\u003eRunning\u003c/code\u003e and the cluster\nprovisions normally.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\n\u003ch2 class=\"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold\" data-sourcepos=\"70:1-70:20;3081-3100\"\u003eEXPECTED RESULTS\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\u003cp class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\" data-sourcepos=\"72:1-75:11;3102-3367\"\u003eSelecting a \"For CKS\" template in Advanced Settings should behave the same as the\ndefault template path: the node Instance transitions \u003ccode class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\"\u003eStarting\u003c/code\u003e → \u003ccode class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\"\u003eRunning\u003c/code\u003e within the\nnormal VM start window, after which CKS provisioning proceeds and the cluster reaches\n\u003ccode class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\"\u003eRunning\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch2 class=\"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold\" data-sourcepos=\"77:1-77:18;3369-3386\"\u003eACTUAL RESULTS\u003c/h2\u003e\n\n\u003cp class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\" data-sourcepos=\"79:1-79:57;3388-3444\"\u003eBehaviour depends solely on the node template selection:\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv class=\"overflow-x-auto w-full px-2 mb-6\" data-sourcepos=\"81:1-85:106;3446-3800\"\u003e\n\nPlain Instance deployed from cks-ubuntu-2204-kvm (no CKS) | Reaches Running — works\nCKS node from default SystemVM template systemvm-kvm-4.22.0-x86_64 | Reaches Running, cluster provisions — works\nCKS node from selected cks-ubuntu-2204-kvm template | Instance stuck in Starting indefinitely\n\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003cp class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\" data-sourcepos=\"87:1-87:21;3802-3822\"\u003eIn the failing case:\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cul class=\"[li_\u0026amp;]:mb-0 [li_\u0026amp;]:mt-1 [li_\u0026amp;]:gap-1 [\u0026amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [\u0026amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3\" data-sourcepos=\"89:1-95:47;3824-4284\"\u003e\n\u003cli class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\" data-sourcepos=\"89:1-90:40;3824-3951\"\u003eThe control node Instance remains in \u003ccode class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\"\u003eStarting\u003c/code\u003e (VM lifecycle state) indefinitely, so\nthe cluster also stays in \u003ccode class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\"\u003eStarting\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\" data-sourcepos=\"91:1-92:26;3952-4065\"\u003eThe libvirt domain is genuinely running on the KVM host: the VNC console is reachable\nand the guest OS boots.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\" data-sourcepos=\"93:1-95:47;4066-4284\"\u003eSSH to the node (port 2222) is not usable; the UI-displayed password is not accepted\non the VNC console (consistent with the node never being marked Running and/or the\nstart/provisioning workflow not completing).\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\n\n### versions\n\nHypervisor version: KVM Ubuntu 24.04\nACS version: 4.22.1.0\nManagement server: Ubuntu 24.04\n\n### The steps to reproduce the bug\n\n_No response_\n\n### What to do about it?\n\n_No response_","comments":4,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13471/comments","created_at":"2026-06-22T23:47:23Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13471/events","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/13471","id":4721416566,"labels":[{"color":"0db7ed","default":false,"description":"","id":1700119912,"name":"component:kubernetes","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzAwMTE5OTEy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:kubernetes"},{"color":"E95420","default":false,"description":"","id":2051004353,"name":"distro:ubuntu","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMDUxMDA0MzUz","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/distro:ubuntu"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13471/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":{"closed_issues":114,"created_at":"2026-04-13T07:02:43Z","creator":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12028987?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sureshanaparti","id":12028987,"login":"sureshanaparti","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDI4OTg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti"},"description":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/46","id":15514689,"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/46/labels","node_id":"MI_kwDOAJTq2M4A7LxB","number":46,"open_issues":252,"sta