itHub.\r\nAlso test if the latest release and main branch are affected too.\r\nAlways add information AFTER of these HTML comments, but no need to delete the comments.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n##### ISSUE TYPE\r\n\u003c!-- Pick one below and delete the rest --\u003e\r\n * Improvement Request / Future request\r\n\r\n##### COMPONENT NAME\r\n\u003c!--\r\nCategorize the issue, e.g. API, VR, VPN, UI, etc.\r\n--\u003e\r\n~~~\r\nAPI\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\r\n\u003c!--\r\nNew line separated list of affected versions, commit ID for issues on main branch.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n4.18.1.0\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CONFIGURATION\r\n\u003c!--\r\nInformation about the configuration if relevant, e.g. basic network, advanced networking, etc.  N/A otherwise\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\nN/A\r\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\r\n\u003c!--\r\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\r\n--\u003e\r\nN/A\r\n\r\n##### SUMMARY\r\n\u003c!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly --\u003e\r\n\r\nRequest to improve updateNetwork api to add/change ipv6 CIRD, ipv6 gate, ipv6 end ,start ip, router ipv6. \r\n\r\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\r\n\u003c!--\r\nFor bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case. Use Screenshots if accurate.\r\n\r\nFor new features, show how the feature would be used.\r\n--\u003e\r\nCreate ipv4 only guest network. Try to add ipv6 CIDR, gateway, start ip, end ip. \r\n\u003c!-- Paste example playbooks or commands between quotes below --\u003e\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- You can also paste gist.github.com links for larger files --\u003e\r\n\r\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\r\n\u003c!-- What did you expect to happen when running the steps above? --\u003e\r\nPossibility to change the settings described above using the interface or api\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\r\n\u003c!-- What actually happened? --\u003e\r\nYou won't be able to do this either through the interface or the api\r\n\u003c!-- Paste verbatim command output between quotes below --\u003e\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n","comments":0,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8304/comments","created_at":"2023-12-05T10:34:13Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8304/events","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/8304","id":2025868922,"labels":[{"color":"1DB401","default":false,"description":"","id":584073853,"name":"component:api","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1ODQwNzM4NTM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:api"},{"color":"f9d0c4","default":false,"description":"","id":592559219,"name":"component:networking","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1OTI1NTkyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:networking"},{"color":"a5f9ff","default":false,"description":"","id":817420428,"name":"type:improvement","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4MTc0MjA0Mjg=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:improvement"},{"color":"C744C9","default":false,"description":"","id":4507982790,"name":"ipv6","node_id":"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAABDLJbxg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/ipv6"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8304/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":{"closed_issues":36,"created_at":"2026-05-08T06:15:20Z","creator":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57355700?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/weizhouapache","id":57355700,"login":"weizhouapache","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MzU1NzAw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache"},"description":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/47","id":15843055,"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/47/labels","node_id":"MI_kwDOAJTq2M4A8b7v","number":47,"open_issues":272,"state":"open","title":"24.0","updated_at":"2026-09-29T10:27:41Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/47"},"node_id":"I_kwDOAJTq2M54wE56","number":8304,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8304/reactions"},"repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack","state":"open","title":"Request to improve updateNetwork api ","type":{"color":"blue","created_at":"2024-01-25T09:11:09Z","description":"A request, idea, or new functionality","id":93574,"name":"Feature","node_id":"IT_kwDNuP_OAAFthg","updated_at":"2024-10-08T08:30:20Z"},"updated_at":"2026-06-29T08:12:58Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8304","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3714094?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/0sorkon","id":3714094,"login":"0sorkon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MTQwOTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0sorkon"}},{"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"### problem\n\nWhen multiple network tiers are brought up in quick succession in a redundant VPC, I can consistently reproduce both VPCs going primary.\n\nThis is really bad because the VIP is then owned by both Virtual Routers and it means traffic is getting dropped like crazy, it makes the entire VPC unusable.  Restarting the VPC recovers it to a good state.\n\nPlease see the comments for debugging information, but in short it appears at least one of the nodes ends up getting munged address information which causes the wrong ips to be programmed on interfaces and the keepalived configs to diverge between nodes which causes the dual primary.  The underlying cause of the issue is this munged address information.\n\n### versions\n\n4.21.0\n\n### The steps to reproduce the bug\n\nUse Terraform to create the VPC, network tiers, and VM Instances.\nTerraform configuration being used is here: https://github.com/bradh352/terraform-config\n\n\n### What to do about it?\n\n_No response_","comments":23,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/11710/comments","created_at":"2025-09-24T13:00:55Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/11710/events","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/11710","id":3449343635,"labels":[{"color":"ffaaeb","default":false,"description":"","id":584073391,"name":"component:virtual-router","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1ODQwNzMzOTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:virtual-router"},{"color":"906C28","default":false,"description":"","id":2694797573,"name":"status:needs-investigation","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjk0Nzk3NTcz","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/status:needs-investigation"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/11710/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":{"closed_issues":114,"created_at":"2026-04-13T07:02:43Z","creator":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12028987?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sureshanaparti","id":12028987,"login":"sureshanaparti","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDI4OTg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti"},"description":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/46","id":15514689,"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/46/labels","node_id":"MI_kwDOAJTq2M4A7LxB","number":46,"open_issues":252,"state":"open","title":"4.22.2","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:13:59Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/46"},"node_id":"I_kwDOAJTq2M7NmM6T","number":11710,"reactions":{"+1":1,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":1,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/11710/reactions"},"repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack","state":"open","title":"Redundant VPC VR goes dual PRIMARY (race condition?)","type":{"color":"red","created_at":"2024-01-25T09:11:09Z","description":"An unexpected problem or behavior","id":93570,"name":"Bug","node_id":"IT_kwDNuP_OAAFtgg","updated_at":"2024-07-26T10:04:57Z"},"updated_at":"2026-09-10T19:50:35Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/11710","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19732188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradh352/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradh352/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradh352/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradh352/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bradh352","id":19732188,"login":"bradh352","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NzMyMTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradh352/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradh352/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradh352/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradh352/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradh352/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bradh352"}},{"author_association":"NONE","body":"### problem\n\nWe did some manual, routing corrections as a work around but want to know if this is a Bug.\n!\nI have the management on a vxlan, but when creating the Zone the system adds the IPs to a VLAN://untagged. that VLAN is for public.\n!\nThere is no way for me to move them to VXLAN the Management:\n!\n!\n!\nThe Management Interface was created during the Installation: But was loaded to a vlan://untagged - I do not have how as I specifically set for vxlan on cloudbr1\n!\n\n\u003cimg width=\"776\" height=\"388\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d297ee4d-6b14-4ddb-82c2-2fe4e1005a59\" /\u003e\n!\n!\n!\nThe Zone Has VXLANs for Primary storage, Management, and Guest.\n!\n\n\u003cimg width=\"610\" height=\"412\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a2115ea3-f395-4076-a4fd-69d1f9eb970c\" /\u003e\n!\n!\n\u003cimg width=\"786\" height=\"401\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6ea626b2-9106-4ae6-ad3d-f368b7a70ea6\" /\u003e\n!\n!\n!\nAny Attemp to change the VLAN to VXLAN results on an error:\n!\n\n\u003cimg width=\"318\" height=\"94\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4adc2cab-aa97-4de4-b951-ff83360e7ef4\" /\u003e\n!\n!\n! Additionally The Secondary Storage is affected by this routing.\n!\n!\nIs the Storage Traffic type solely for Primary storage ? I will like to have the secondary storage on a separate routed or L2/Vlan tagged\nOur primary Storage is CEPH running on VXLAN and have no problems at all - Primary storage and Guest VXLAN are the only thing working as it should per the documentation.\n!\n!\n\n\u003cimg width=\"612\" height=\"350\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7d4acb42-b211-4b83-8f8a-e7fbb016c0f9\" /\u003e\n\n\n\n### versions\n\nCS 4.20.1\nPRI STORAGE:   CEPH\nSEC STORAGE: NFS EMC\nVXLAN\nForced VLAN for Public - but System auto-configures the Management on vlan://untagged which also uses Secondary Storage.\n\n### The steps to reproduce the bug\n\n1. Create a new Zone, all new systems.\n2. put on vxlan management, secondary-storage and guest on cloudbr1\n3. pod settings: Assign the IP range for management - there is nowhere to add a VXLAN ports for Management during the initial setup/configuration\n4. System VM proxy have to be routed manually, same as Secondary storage.\n\n\nNot possible to set secondary storage using routing without VRFs, as systemVM automatically try to push it over VLAN://untagged being forced to manually route over vlan://untagged...\n\nAs a workaround we route sec Storage and Management over vlan://untagged\n\n### What to do about it?\n\nThe management should use the vxlan://assigend, and secondary storage should be able to have its own route if needed.\nThe UI configures the Storage for the primary Storage only.\n","comments":11,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/11983/comments","created_at":"2025-11-04T21:15:43Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/11983/events","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/11983","id":3588173816,"labels":[{"color":"f9d0c4","default":false,"description":"","id":592559219,"name":"component:networking","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1OTI1NTkyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:networking"},{"color":"99fcc4","default":false,"description":"VXLAN","id":1134705229,"name":"component:vxlan","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTM0NzA1MjI5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:vxlan"},{"color":"4471c4","default":false,"description":"","id":1150675549,"name":"type:new-feature","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTUwNjc1NTQ5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:new-feature"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/11983/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":{"closed_issues":1302,"created_at":"2021-01-04T09:07:50Z","creator":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2486961?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DaanHoogland","id":2486961,"login":"DaanHoogland","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODY5NjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland"},"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/19","id":6265435,"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19/labels","node_id":"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lNjI2NTQzNQ==","number":19,"open_issues":185,"state":"open","title":"unplanned","updated_at":"2026-09-24T11:01:33Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19"},"node_id":"I_kwDOAJTq2M7V3y_4","number":11983,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/11983/reactions"},"repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack","state":"open","title":"CS 4.20.1 Unable to run Management and secondary Storage on VXLAN - System AutoConfigures ON VLAN Untagged: the VXLAN Management and SecondaryStorage Forced to run on VLAN://untagged","type":{"color":"blue","created_at":"2024-01-25T09:11:09Z","description":"A request, idea, or new functionality","id":93574,"name":"Feature","node_id":"IT_kwDNuP_OAAFthg","updated_at":"2024-10-08T08:30:20Z"},"updated_at":"2026-07-01T14:21:09Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/11983","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10108973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tatay188/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tatay188/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tatay188/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tatay188/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tatay188","id":10108973,"login":"tatay188","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTA4OTcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tatay188/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tatay188/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tatay188/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tatay188/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tatay188/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tatay188"}},{"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"\u003c!--\r\nVerify first that your issue/request is not already reported on GitHub.\r\nAlso test if the latest release and master branch are affected too.\r\nAlways add information AFTER of these HTML comments, but no need to delete the comments.\r\n--\u003e\r\nAbility to define IP address beside of choosing VMs in Static NAT, Port Forward and Load balancer services to provide those services to servers outside of CloudStack.\r\n##### ISSUE TYPE\r\n\u003c!-- Pick one below and delete the rest --\u003e\r\n * Feature Idea\r\n\r\n##### COMPONENT NAME\r\n\u003c!--\r\nCategorize the issue, e.g. API, VR, VPN, UI, etc.\r\n--\u003e\r\n~~~\r\nVR\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\r\n\u003c!--\r\nNew line separated list of affected versions, commit ID for issues on master branch.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n~~~\r\nAll versions\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CONFIGURATION\r\n\u003c!--\r\nInformation about the configuration if relevant, e.g. basic network, advanced networking, etc.  N/A otherwise\r\n--\u003e\r\nAdvanced networking\r\n\r\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\r\n\u003c!--\r\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\r\n--\u003e\r\nN/A\r\n\r\n##### SUMMARY\r\n\u003c!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly --\u003e\r\n\r\nIn some network services we need to specify which VM should use it. For example Static NAT, Port Forward and Load balancer.\r\nIt would be a good idea if we can also specify IP address of a server which is not managed by CloudStack.\r\nThis feature helps us to use network services provided by virtual router for physical servers or even VMs outside of CloudStack management area but share a common L2 network with other VMs in CloudStack.\r\nThis feature also requires reserve IP address capability in all type of networks. We can expand the issue #4357 for private IPs in isolated networks too.\r\n\r\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\r\n\u003c!--\r\nFor bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case. Use Screenshots if accurate.\r\n\r\nFor new features, show how the feature would be used.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- Paste example playbooks or commands between quotes below --\u003e\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n1. Create an isolated network\r\n2. In Port forward section define a new rule\r\n3. In \"Add VM\" panel write IP address of the server outside of CloudStack\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- You can also paste gist.github.com links for larger files --\u003e\r\n\r\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\r\n\u003c!-- What did you expect to happen when running the steps above? --\u003e\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\nAn iptables rule created in virtual router to forward desired port to the server IP\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\r\n\u003c!-- What actually happened? --\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- Paste verbatim command output between quotes below --\u003e\r\n~~~\r\n\r\nIt is not possible to mention IP address of the server outside of CloudStack\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n","comments":26,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/4542/comments","created_at":"2020-12-14T13:58:37Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/4542/events","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/4542","id":766468471,"labels":[{"color":"f9d0c4","default":false,"description":"","id":592559219,"name":"component:networking","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1OTI1NTkyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:networking"},{"color":"c1fca4","default":false,"description":"","id":2249631279,"name":"type:experimental-feature","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMjQ5NjMxMjc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:experimental-feature"},{"color":"000088","default":false,"description":"a 