ete the comments.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n##### ISSUE TYPE\r\n\u003c!-- Pick one below and delete the rest --\u003e\r\n * Bug Report\r\n\r\n##### COMPONENT NAME\r\n\u003c!--\r\nCategorize the issue, e.g. API, VR, VPN, UI, etc.\r\n--\u003e\r\n~~~\r\nUI\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\r\n\u003c!--\r\nNew line separated list of affected versions, commit ID for issues on main branch.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n4.17.0\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CONFIGURATION\r\n\u003c!--\r\nInformation about the configuration if relevant, e.g. basic network, advanced networking, etc.  N/A otherwise\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\nN/A\r\n\r\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\r\n\u003c!--\r\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n\r\n##### SUMMARY\r\n\u003c!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly --\u003e\r\n\r\nUnable to Set Password Complexity requirement to include special characters \r\n\r\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\r\n\u003c!--\r\nFor bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case. Use Screenshots if accurate.\r\n\r\nFor new features, show how the feature would be used.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\nOur organization wants to enforce password requirements upon password resets on the VM. The default password requirement is 6 characters. I have updated that to 14 characters using vm.password.length\r\n\r\nHowever, there is no provision to enforce inclusion of select special characters (like !@#%^\u0026*()-) -- exclude the $\r\n\r\nIs there some way to achieve this? \r\n\r\n\u003c!-- Paste example playbooks or commands between quotes below --\u003e\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- You can also paste gist.github.com links for larger files --\u003e\r\n\r\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\r\n\u003c!-- What did you expect to happen when running the steps above? --\u003e\r\n\r\n~~~\r\nOur organization wants to enforce password requirements upon password resets on the VM. The default password requirement is 6 characters. I have updated that to 14 characters using vm.password.length\r\n\r\nHowever, there is no provision to enforce inclusion of select special characters (like !@#%^\u0026*()-) -- exclude the $\r\n\r\nIs there some way to achieve this? \r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\r\n\u003c!-- What actually happened? --\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- Paste verbatim command output between quotes below --\u003e\r\n~~~\r\nPassword reset only includes numbers, upper and lower case\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n","comments":26,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6861/comments","created_at":"2022-11-01T17:57:01Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6861/events","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/6861","id":1431841155,"labels":[{"color":"4471c4","default":false,"description":"","id":1150675549,"name":"type:new-feature","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTUwNjc1NTQ5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:new-feature"},{"color":"E43179","default":false,"description":"","id":6890295339,"name":"status:stale","node_id":"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAABmrGQKw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/status:stale"},{"color":"ededed","default":false,"id":9849008471,"name":"no-issue-activity","node_id":"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAACSwvxVw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/no-issue-activity"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6861/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":{"closed_issues":1302,"created_at":"2021-01-04T09:07:50Z","creator":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2486961?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DaanHoogland","id":2486961,"login":"DaanHoogland","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODY5NjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland"},"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/19","id":6265435,"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19/labels","node_id":"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lNjI2NTQzNQ==","number":19,"open_issues":185,"state":"open","title":"unplanned","updated_at":"2026-09-24T11:01:33Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19"},"node_id":"I_kwDOAJTq2M5VWCmD","number":6861,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6861/reactions"},"repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack","state":"open","title":"VM Password reset - Unable to set Password Complexity requirement for Special Characters","updated_at":"2026-05-27T02:18:38Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6861","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71042351?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nxsbi","id":71042351,"login":"nxsbi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMDQyMzUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi"}},{"author_association":"NONE","body":"\u003c!--\r\nVerify first that your issue/request is not already reported on GitHub.\r\nAlso test if the latest release and main branch are affected too.\r\nAlways add information AFTER of these HTML comments, but no need to delete the comments.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n##### ISSUE TYPE\r\n\u003c!-- Pick one below and delete the rest --\u003e\r\n * Bug Report\r\n\r\n##### COMPONENT NAME\r\n\u003c!--\r\nCategorize the issue, e.g. API, VR, VPN, UI, etc.\r\n--\u003e\r\n~~~\r\nCompute Cluster UI\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\r\n\u003c!--\r\nNew line separated list of affected versions, commit ID for issues on main branch.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n4.19.1.1\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CONFIGURATION\r\n\u003c!--\r\nInformation about the configuration if relevant, e.g. basic network, advanced networking, etc.  N/A otherwise\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n\r\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\r\n\u003c!--\r\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n\r\n##### SUMMARY\r\n\u003c!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly --\u003e\r\n\r\nWe have 2 Compute Clusters:\r\n\r\n- Cluster 1 : Oversubcription = 1\r\n- Cluster 2 : Oversubcription = 2\r\n\r\nRefering to the screenshot below, Cluster 1 is showing the correct No. of CPU Cores allocated. \r\n\r\nBut for Cluster 2, it seems inaccurate. The number of allocation exceeded whats available. Resulting in a UI error. \r\n\r\n![Screenshot 2024-09-17 at 10 23 55 PM](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/36c46ff6-7d2a-4641-80e5-48e28e040ad0)\r\n\r\n![Screenshot 2024-09-17 at 10 24 05 PM](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/68972682-4bf4-41d4-8d4e-d61b82132c35)\r\n\r\nBut the bigger problem now, is that both clusters have exceeded the allocation threshold, but there was no notification sent. And neither did cloudstack stop users from creating new virtual machines from the clusters.\r\n\r\nWithout this, Admins would not be able to ensure n+1 sufficient capacity in the event of a node failure. \r\n\r\n![Screenshot 2024-09-17 at 10 34 14 PM](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/550f0ab7-dc3b-4fbf-b757-75153761b17c)\r\n\r\nIn summary, there are 3 Issues:\r\n\r\n- No. Of Allocated CPU Cores should display the full available amount, after oversubscription\r\n- Admin should get Notification if exceeded the global setting threshold (cluster.cpu.allocated.capacity.notificationthreshold)\r\n- User should not be able to create resources into the cluster after exceeding global setting threshold (cluster.cpu.allocated.capacity.disablethreshold)\r\n\r\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\r\n\u003c!--\r\nFor bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case. Use Screenshots if accurate.\r\n\r\nFor new features, show how the feature would be used.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- Paste example playbooks or commands between quotes below --\u003e\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- You can also paste gist.github.com links for larger files --\u003e\r\n\r\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\r\n\u003c!-- What did you expect to happen when running the steps above? --\u003e\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n- No. Of Allocated CPU Cores should display the full available amount, after oversubscription\r\n- Admin should get Notification if exceeded the global setting threshold (cluster.cpu.allocated.capacity.notificationthreshold)\r\n- User should not be able to create resources into the cluster after exceeding global setting threshold (cluster.cpu.allocated.capacity.disablethreshold)\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\r\n\u003c!-- What actually happened? --\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- Paste verbatim command output between quotes below --\u003e\r\n~~~\r\n- No. Of Allocated CPU Cores should not displaying total available cores correctly, after oversubscription.\r\n- Admin did not get Notification if exceeded the global setting threshold (cluster.cpu.allocated.capacity.notificationthreshold)\r\n- User is able to create resources into the cluster after exceeding global setting threshold (cluster.cpu.allocated.capacity.disablethreshold)\r\n~~~\r\n","comments":12,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/9693/comments","created_at":"2024-09-17T14:38:58Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/9693/events","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/9693","id":2531348246,"labels":[{"color":"951862","default":false,"description":"","id":2630836378,"name":"status:needs-functional-definition","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjMwODM2Mzc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/status:needs-functional-definition"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/9693/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":{"closed_issues":1302,"created_at":"2021-01-04T09:07:50Z","creator":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2486961?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DaanHoogland","id":2486961,"login":"DaanHoogland","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODY5NjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland"},"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/19","id":6265435,"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19/labels","node_id":"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lNjI2NTQzNQ==","number":19,"open_issues":185,"state":"open","title":"unplanned","updated_at":"2026-09-24T11:01:33Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19"},"node_id":"I_kwDOAJTq2M6W4U8W","number":9693,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/9693/reactions"},"repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack","state":"open","title":"No. of CPU Cores in Compute Cluster doesnt display correctly when Cluster has oversubscription more than 1","updated_at":"2026-09-07T01:45:36Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/9693","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/147712084?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btzq/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btzq/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btzq/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btzq/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/btzq","id":147712084,"login":"btzq","node_id":"U_kgDOCM3oVA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btzq/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btzq/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btzq/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btzq/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btzq/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/btzq"}},{"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"\u003c!--\r\nVerify first that your issue/request is not already reported on GitHub.\r\nAlso test if the latest release and main branch are affected too.\r\nAlways add information AFTER of these HTML comments, but no need to delete the comments.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n##### ISSUE TYPE\r\n\u003c!-- Pick one below and delete the rest --\u003e\r\n * Documentation Report\r\n * testing/CI\r\n\r\n##### COMPONENT NAME\r\n\u003c!--\r\nCategorize the issue, e.g. API, VR, VPN, UI, etc.\r\n--\u003e\r\n~~~\r\nmarvin\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\r\n\u003c!--\r\nNew line separated list of affected versions, commit ID for issues on main branch.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n4.18\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CONFIGURATION\r\n\u003c!--\r\nInformation about the configuration if relevant, e.g. basic network, advanced networking, etc.  N/A otherwise\r\n--\u003e\r\n~~~\r\nadvanced zone with security groups.\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\r\n\u003c!--\r\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n\r\n##### SUMMARY\r\n\u003c!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly --\u003e\r\nwhen an advanced zone with security groups is used to test for regressions, a lot of errors occur.\r\nan example\r\n```\r\nERROR: test suite for \u003cclass 'tests.smoke.test_router_dns.TestRouterDns'\u003e\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.6/site-packages/nose/suite.py\", line 210, in run\r\n    self.setUp()\r\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.6/site-packages/nose/suite.py\", line 293, in setUp\r\n    self.setupContext(ancestor)\r\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.6/site-packages/nose/suite.py\", line 316, in setupContext\r\n    try_run(context, names)\r\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.6/site-packages/nose/util.py\", line 471, in try_run\r\n    return func()\r\n  File \"/marvin/tests/smoke/test_router_dns.py\", line 92, in setUpClass\r\n    zoneid=cls.zone.id)\r\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.6/site-packages/marvin/lib/base.py\", line 3562, in create\r\n    return Network(apiclient.createNetwork(cmd).__dict__)\r\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.6/site-packages/marvin/cloudstackAPI/cloudstackAPIClient.py\", line 2981, in createNetwork\r\n    response = self.connection.marvinRequest(command, response_type=response, method=method)\r\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.6/site-packages/marvin/cloudstackConnection.py\", line 381, in marvinRequest\r\n    raise e\r\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.6/site-packages/marvin/cloudstackConnection.py\", line 376, in marvinRequest\r\n    raise self.__lastError\r\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.6/site-packages/marvin/cloudstackConnection.py\", line 310, in __parseAndGetResponse\r\n    response_cls)\r\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.6/site-packages/marvin/jsonHelper.py\", line 155, in getResultObj\r\n    raise cloudstackException.CloudstackAPIException(respname, errMsg)\r\nmarvin.cloudstackException.CloudstackAPIException: Execute cmd: createnetwork failed, due to: errorCode: 431, errorText:Only shared guest network can be created in security group enabled zone\r\n```\r\n\r\nthis is not necessary as we know beforehand that these tests will fail.\r\nTests need to be properly tagged to not run in these environments.\r\n\r\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\r\n\u003c!--\r\nFor bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case. Use Screenshots if accurate.\r\n\r\nFor new features, show how the feature would be used.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- Paste example playbooks or commands between quotes below --\u003e\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- You can also paste gist.github.com links for larger files --\u003e\r\n\r\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\r\n\u003c!-- What did you expect to happen when running the steps above? --\u003e\r\n\r\n~~~\r\ntest will not run\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\r\n\u003c!-- What actually happened? --\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- Paste verbatim command output between quotes below --\u003e\r\n~~~\r\ntest runs and fails\r\n~~~\r\n","comments":8,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/7155/comments","created_at":"2023-02-01T10:22:04Z","events_url":"ht